<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18080" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fīcārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		ficus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to figs</i>, <i>fig-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crates,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 48, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">culices,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 35, 41, § 118</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vasa, Paul. ex Fest. s. v. ‡ ORCA,
					p. 180 Müll.: Fauni (perh. so called on account of
					their rank luxuriance),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Iesai. 5, 13, 21</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fīcārĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>a fig
			plantation</i>, <i><span class="en">Pall. 4, 10,
			28</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>An island near Sardinia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 7,
				13, § 34</span></i>.</div>
